# Copy to .env (gitignored) or inject via CI secrets / secrets Gradle plugin.
# Never commit real secrets (API keys, client_secret). OAuth client IDs are public identifiers.

# Optional Gemini / Firebase AI
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Google OAuth Web client ID (GoogleDriveAuth / requestIdToken)
# Project: thevvforg (1058219630435)
# Register an Android OAuth client for package com.vvf.smartmanager using the
# actual SHA-1 fingerprint of the signing certificate used by each build.
# The previously embedded debug keystore was removed; its old SHA-1 is no longer reliable.
# Verify the Gradle-managed debug certificate and the release/upload certificate separately.
# Confirmed in Google Cloud project thevvforg: OAuth client named "Drive Semantic Search Web".
# Google's Android ID-token flow requires the backend/server WEB client ID here;
# pair it with an Android OAuth client matching package + actual signing SHA-1.
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID="1058219630435-4dfjaes61070ut8t8vvki51cc7ln5n7r.apps.googleusercontent.com"
